# Copy to .env — see root README "Meta Pixel + Conversions API"

# Meta Conversions API (optional — same Pixel ID as VITE_META_PIXEL_ID on the web app)
# META_PIXEL_ID=123456789012345
# META_CONVERSIONS_API_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# META_TEST_EVENT_CODE=

# Web app origin (used in CAPI event_source_url fallbacks)
# WEB_URL=http://localhost:5173

# ── Google Analytics 4 — Data API (admin dashboard Traffic tab) ──────────────
# GA4_PROPERTY_ID  Numeric property ID (GA4 Admin → Property Settings → Property ID)
# GA4_PROPERTY_ID=123456789

# Auth — choose ONE of the two methods:

# Method A: Service account (if your Google/GCP org allows adding it to GA4)
#   1. Create a service account in GCP Console → IAM → Service Accounts
#   2. Download the JSON key
#   3. In GA4: Admin → Property Access Management → Add users → paste the
#      client_email from the JSON (must be Viewer or higher)
#   4. Paste the entire key JSON as a single-line string below:
# GA4_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=

# Method B: OAuth 2.0 refresh token (recommended — uses your own Google account)
#   1. GCP Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → Create OAuth client ID
#      → Application type: Desktop app
#   2. Download the client ID + secret
#   3. Run once:  npx tsx apps/api/scripts/ga4-get-refresh-token.ts
#      Follow the printed URL, authorize, paste the code → your refresh token is printed
#   4. Fill in the three vars below:
# GA4_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GA4_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GA4_OAUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN=
